# modules/sast/rules/crypto.rules - docs/DESIGN.md §6.3 "crypto.rules" seed
# catalog: MD5/SHA1 for security, DES/ECB, hardcoded IV/salt, disabled TLS
# verification, Math.random() for tokens.

id: SAST-CRY-WEAK_HASH-01
title: MD5 or SHA1 used where a security-relevant hash is expected
severity: medium
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-327
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: (hashlib\.md5|hashlib\.sha1|MessageDigest\.getInstance\(["'](MD5|SHA-?1)["']\)|crypto\.createHash\(["'](md5|sha1)["']\))
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Use SHA-256 or better for anything security-relevant (password hashing needs
  a dedicated KDF such as bcrypt/scrypt/argon2, not a bare fast hash at all).
  MD5 and SHA1 remain acceptable only for non-adversarial checksums.
references: CWE-327

id: SAST-CRY-DES_ECB-01
title: DES or ECB-mode cipher in use
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-327
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: (DES/ECB|AES/ECB|MODE_ECB)
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: Replace DES with AES-256, and replace ECB mode with an authenticated mode
  such as GCM. ECB leaks structure across blocks of identical plaintext regardless of
  which cipher it wraps.
references: CWE-327

id: SAST-CRY-HARDCODED_IV-01
title: Hardcoded initialization vector or salt
severity: medium
confidence: low
cwe: CWE-329
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: [Ii][Vv][[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*b?["'][0-9A-Fa-f]{16,}["']
dialect: ere
tags: static
severity-floor: low
remediation: Generate the IV/salt fresh per operation with a cryptographically secure
  random source, and store it alongside the ciphertext rather than fixing it in source.
references: CWE-329

id: SAST-CRY-TLS_VERIFY_DISABLED-01
title: TLS certificate verification disabled
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-295
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: (verify[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*False|rejectUnauthorized[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*false|InsecureSkipVerify[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true|ssl_verify[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*[Ff]alse)
dialect: ere
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Never disable certificate verification outside a throwaway local test fixture.
  If a private CA is in play, add it to the trust store instead of turning verification off.
references: CWE-295

id: SAST-CRY-WEAK_RANDOM_TOKEN-01
title: Math.random() used to generate a token, session id, or secret
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-338
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: Math\.random\(\)
dialect: ere
context-require: (token|Token|session|Session|password|Password|secret|Secret|auth|Auth)
context-window: 3
tags: static
remediation: Use a cryptographically secure random source (crypto.randomBytes /
  crypto.getRandomValues) for anything used as a token, session id, or secret.
  Math.random() is not unpredictable enough to resist a determined attacker.
references: CWE-338
